# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line-ending policy — D-41
#
# This project verifies artifacts by exact SHA-256 bytes (ingestion manifests,
# proposal evidence, pinned readiness receipts, offline bundles). Git's
# core.autocrlf, which defaults to `true` on Git for Windows, rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. Every affected checksum then mismatches and the
# fail-closed provenance layer correctly rejects its own committed inputs.
#
# Observed on 2026-07-29: with core.autocrlf=true, 762 of 859 tracked files
# differed from their committed blobs and 21 tests failed for this reason
# alone. Enumerating individual files (the previous approach) does not scale
# and had already missed most of the repository.
#
# The rule below makes checkout byte-identical to the committed blob on every
# platform, independent of each developer's git config. Correctness must not
# depend on local settings.
#
# After changing this file, refresh an existing checkout with:
#     git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard      # working tree only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default: detect text, store LF, and CHECK OUT LF on all platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never touched by any line-ending or diff filter.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.docx    binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.parquet binary
*.zip     binary
*.gz      binary
*.tif     binary
*.tiff    binary
*.pth     binary
*.onnx    binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-exact artifacts.
#
# These are already covered by the `* text=auto eol=lf` default. They are kept
# listed explicitly because each one is bound by a SHA-256 recorded in a
# manifest or receipt: if a future edit relaxes the default, these must still
# never be rewritten. Treat this block as a tripwire, not as redundancy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/mae_sai_priority_subdistricts.geojson   -text
outputs/mae_sai_facility_context.csv            -text
outputs/mae_sai_population_nodes.csv            -text
outputs/mae_sai_access_edges.csv                -text
outputs/mae_sai_scenario_inputs_manifest.json   -text
outputs/ait_vap001_reference_candidate.json     -text
outputs/cdse_hat_yai_2025_metadata.csv          -text
outputs/real_data_ingestion_manifest.csv        -text
services/api/data/study_area_bundles/*.json     -text
apps/web/public/offline-demo/mae-sai/*.json     -text

# Proposal evidence is checksummed byte-for-byte and must survive clean checkouts.
docs/submission/2026-geohackathon/**/*.md                       -text
docs/submission/2026-geohackathon/**/*.json                     -text
packages/contracts/examples/proposal-evidence.fixture-demo.json -text
services/geoai-runner/evidence/*.json                           -text
docs/validation/controlled_three_model_gate_receipt.json        -text
docs/validation/controlled_three_model_acquisition_manifest.csv -text
